# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Game data must never be committed.
#
# This project is built around you supplying your own legally obtained ROM. It
# never ships game data, and the rules below are the mechanism, not a courtesy:
# a built .nds is a complete copy of a commercial game, and build/ reaches well
# over a gigabyte in normal use.
#
# What IS safe to distribute is a .bps patch — a delta that is useless without
# the player's own ROM — but they are produced into build/ alongside the ROMs,
# so attach them to a release rather than committing them.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Built ROMs, patches and their reports (reports embed local absolute paths).
# Leading slash matters: a bare `build/` would also exclude tools/build/, which is the
# entire build pipeline.
/build/

# Anything that is, or came out of, a ROM
*.nds
*.bps
*.sav
*.dsv
*.herf
*.tlk
*.gda
*.itm
*.2da
*.are
*.plo
*.spl
*.ncgr
*.nclr
*.nsbmd
*.nsbca
*.emit

# Emulator state
*.ds[0-9]
*.dst
/Battery/

# Scratch space
/work/
/scratch/
/tmp/

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/

# Local backups made before risky edits — useful to keep on disk, noise in a repo
*.bak
*.before-*
*.blank-backup

# Assistant instructions — kept on disk, deliberately not published. These are
# operating rules written for an AI collaborator, not documentation for users.
CLAUDE.md

# Editors and OS
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Built presets, written by the GUI when you press Build preset.
profiles/presets/_built_*.json

# PyInstaller release output and its scratch dirs. A built folder contains a full
# Python runtime, and any ROM built from inside it lands in dist/.../build/.
/dist/
/build/_pyi/
